    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="letterhead">The Westminster Press <lb/>Witherspoon
                        Building, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__747" type="place">Philadelphia</rs> 7,
                            <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__998" type="place">Pa.</rs></fw><fw
                        place="left" type="adressline">Prof. Paul Tillich <lb/>Union Theological
                        Seminary, <lb/>Broadway at 120th Street, <lb/><rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York</rs> 27, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__865" type="place">New
                            York</rs>.</fw><dateline><date when="1946-06-10">June 10,
                        1946</date>.</dateline><salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Professor Tillich</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>In the Fall we shall publish <rs ref="#tillich__ASPVVH5A" type="work">REVELATION
                        AND REASON</rs>, by <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__300" type="person">Emil
                        Brunner</rs>.</p>
                <p>We are quite anxious that this important work have the widest possible
                    circulation and I am writing to ask if we might have an advance review from you
                    from which we might quote in our advertising. An honorarium, of course, will be
                    in order.</p>
                <p>We can send paper bound page proof now or at any later time you may
                    designate.</p>
                <p>A return addressed post card is enclosed for your convenience and I hope to hear
                    favorably from you.</p>
                <closer><salute>Yours very truly,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__791"
                            type="person">R. Clarke Hannaford <lb/><!-- gedruckt: -->R. Clarke
                        Hannaford</rs> <lb/>Director, <lb/>Merchandising
                    Division</signed><!--links, auf der anderen Seite von <q>Merchandising Division</q>: <q>RCH:F.</q>-->
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
